{:edb/db-before-t 1514 :edb/db-after-t 1515 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534827 50 #inst "2026-10-08T08:15:39.117Z" 13194139534827 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186312769 13194139534827 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186312777 13194139534827 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186312780 13194139534827 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186312762 13194139534827 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186312784 13194139534827 true] [17592186290355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312776 13194139534827 true] [17592186312762 1017 #edb/ref 17592186312763 13194139534827 true] [17592186312762 1089 "q-104065" 13194139534827 true] [17592186312762 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534827 true] [17592186312762 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}.$ Assume that $0<x<\\pi .$" 13194139534827 true] [17592186312762 1113 #uuid "e80102fb-b0d5-5bdb-8b2c-e58b30c1b434" 13194139534827 true] [17592186312762 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+4{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the right-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nwhere $C={C}_{1}+{C}_{2}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})+4{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡1+{\\pi }^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534827 true] [17592186312763 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312764 13194139534827 true] [17592186312763 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312765 13194139534827 true] [17592186312763 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312766 13194139534827 true] [17592186312763 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312767 13194139534827 true] [17592186312763 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312768 13194139534827 true] [17592186312763 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534827 true] [17592186312763 1041 "selection" 13194139534827 true] [17592186312763 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312767 13194139534827 true] [17592186312763 1110 #uuid "9c26e6cf-2d22-5091-8bf9-ee65799df215" 13194139534827 true] [17592186312764 1034 "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+8{x}